+<section id="github-update-20261031" class="status" style="scroll-margin-top:10rem"><h2 style="margin-top:0">31 October follow-up: post-approval changes, retention evidence and interoperability</h2><p>Evidect #27 tests post-approval changes and process observations (37 existing + 43 new tests; eight synthetic cases). VAP #39–#41 and Evidect #22–#26 separate retention deadlines, deletion evidence and receiver review. VAP #1 adds Python/Node interoperability (32 test methods; two positive and six negative vectors). First-party CI counts remain separate by scope.</p><p>Process separation is not independent authority; a reached deadline or CLOSED_REVIEW does not establish deletion success. Proposals and experimental extensions remain <strong>unadopted</strong>; independent third-party reproduction is <strong>not established</strong>. Historical 53-case, 159 / 26 and other records and fixed distributions are preserved.</p><p><a href="https://veritaschain.org/vso/announcements/2026-10-31-retention-runtime-interop-research-update/">Read the three research areas and limits →</a></p></section>
 <section id="github-update-20261030-evening" class="status" style="scroll-margin-top:10rem"><h2 style="margin-top:0">30 October follow-up: evidence preservation, rechecks and guide notices</h2><p>VAP #33 binds publication, disclosure and authorization; #34 covers scoped erasure; #35 preserves 53 original evidence cases and an offline kit; #36 generates bilingual reports; #37 maps 23 requirements and provides review handoff; #38 checks sending prerequisites during collector outage and recovery. VCP guide #3 and #4 distinguish illustrative SDK names from the available SDK, and historical certification procedures from VSO’s current role.</p><p>Runtime checks passed first-party Python 3.12 / 3.14 CI. Saved-evidence rechecks are not fresh runs; automated reports are not human review. Proposals and extensions remain <strong>unadopted</strong>; independent third-party reproduction is <strong>not established</strong>. Erasure is not universal deletion; collector evidence is not independent observation or all-route bypass prevention. Historical tests and fixed distributions remain intact.</p><p><a href="https://veritaschain.org/vso/announcements/2026-10-30-evidence-preservation-collector-review-update/">Read the eight updates and limits →</a></p></section>
 <section id="github-update-20261030" class="status"><h2 style="margin-top:0">30 October: evidence assessment, uploads and authorization research</h2><p>VAP PR #30 proposes evidence bindings; #31 provides an offline assessor (20 test methods; 23/23 matching scenarios); #32 exercises loopback uploads (39 methods; 17/17 upload cases and 17/17 evidence rechecks match). Evidect #20 adds a synthetic authorization gate (37 tests; 18 scenarios); #21 adds optional SQLite replay reservations (33 new tests; 70 gate-specific tests and four process scenarios). Counts remain separate by scope.</p><p>All results are first-party CI checks. Upload case UL-14 shows a <strong>successful bypass outside the gate</strong>, not OS isolation or production bypass prevention. Experimental extensions remain <strong>unadopted</strong>; independent third-party reproduction is <strong>not established</strong>. Historical 159 / 26 and 306 / 140 test records and fixed distributions are preserved.</p><p><a href="https://veritaschain.org/vso/announcements/2026-10-30-incident-evidence-authorization-research-update/">Read the five updates and limits →</a></p></section>
 <section id="github-update-20261029" class="status"><h2 style="margin-top:0">VSO updates SDK evidence checks, the Explorer demo and Evidect reproduction guidance</h2><p>29 October: stricter SDK inputs, an API-connected signed-evidence Explorer route and Evidect reproduction guidance are available. The legacy dashboard and historical 159 / 26 and 306 / 140 test records remain separate. Experimental extensions are <strong>unadopted</strong>; independent reproduction is <strong>not established</strong>.</p><p>The new demo uses signed synthetic evidence; intact full evidence is still INDETERMINATE. The API-disconnected / unsigned description in the 27 October record applies to the legacy dashboard.</p><p><a href="https://veritaschain.org/vso/announcements/2026-10-29-sdk-evidence-demo-reproduction-update/">Read the update and limits →</a> · <a href="https://veritaschain.org/explorer/app/#/evidence-demo">SDK Evidence Demo</a> · <a href="https://evidect.veritaschain.org/methodology/#reproduce">Evidect</a></p></section>
